discovery of a new specimen of iguana in the Galapagos. They went on and on about their expedition to the volcanic islands!<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I just wrote an article about the Galapagos! How funny is that?"}, {"time": "18900", "image": "engenn6le15ob11re2img06.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\"> Vanessa </span>: Yeah, that's weird. I also had a group of musicians who were in town for the jazz festival. The came in after their show and the saxophonist played us a solo. He was \u2026 mesmerizing (dreamy voice)<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Tell me the truth, V. How cute was he?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Vanessa </span>: Very funny, Sally. I'd rather have customers like him than the rude clients I get all the time!"}, {"time": "41200", "image": "engenn6le15ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I guess so. Hey! We should have a party soon, don't you think?    <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Vanessa </span>: I don't know \u2026 I'd rather just have a quiet dinner with you guys.<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Come on! You ought to put more fun in your life! <br>\n<span class=\"strong\"> Vanessa </span>: How big is this party going to be?<br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:Don't worry about that. You might want to invite that saxophonist though!"}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Great Places to Visit"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "All That Jazz"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 15}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Would Rather for What is Preferable"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the expression <span class=\"strong italic\">would rather</span> to ask for or express preference. We generally used its contracted form (<span class=\"strong italic\">'d rather</span>), followed by the basic or infinitive form of the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: <ul><li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I'd rather have customers like him than the rude clients I get all the time!</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I'd rather just have a quiet dinner with you guys.</span></li> </ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: We should have a party soon! <br/><span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: I don't know ... I'd rather just have a quiet dinner. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: Come on! You ought to put more fun in your life!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you're comparing two things or actions, you use the expression <span class=\"strong italic\">than</span>. When you're comparing with verbs, be consistent: don't change the form of the verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I'd rather go to the Jazz festival than stay at home.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">We'd rather have a party with friends than have a quiet afternoon.</span></li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you state preference in relation to another person's actions, that is, if you prefer someone to do something, <span class=\"strong\">you use the verb in the past form</span>.<br/> There is another subject for the second part of the sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I'd rather <span class=\"strong\">you</span> <span class=\"underline\">came</span> home for a party.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">We'd rather <span class=\"strong\">he</span> <span class=\"underline\">played</span> jazz.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I'd rather <span class=\"strong\">they</span> <span class=\"underline\">weren't</span> regular customers.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic product-color-text\">I'd rather <span class=\"strong\">the saxophonist</span> <span class=\"underline\">attended</span> the party.</span></li></ul>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Questions with How + Adjectives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">How + adjective</span> in a question if you want to know how someone or something is."}, {"type": "example", "content": "How funny is that?"}, {"type": "example", "content": " How cute was he?  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "How big is this party going to be?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "biologist "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a scientist who focuses on living organisms "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Darwin was the most influential biologist of his time"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words to review."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "specimen "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an individual example of a species "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In the summer you can see many specimens of wildlife"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "expedition "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a journey with a specific purpose, like exploration or research "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How amazing would it be to take part in an expedition to this remote land"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "volcanic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " relating to a volcano "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Galapagos are an archipelago of volcanic islands"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "solo "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a part in a musical piece where one instrument plays unaccompanied "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This saxophone solo was amazing!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mesmerizing "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "holding someone's attention very intensely "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Jazz performers are mesmerizing-"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le15ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le15ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue (12-14 lines) about your plans for the weekend."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, think of 5 or 6 things to do. Make sure you include: <ul> <li>activities and occasions</li> <li>names of buildings and places</li> </ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " Make suggestions and talk about preferences. Express your disagreement on the activities. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find one suggestion that you both agree on."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your dialogue aloud."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about preferences and make suggestions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask clarifications about things and people."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about celebrations, buildings and special occasions."}]}]}